From 84e1e2b339c0074a521e9816f9aeb96ee720580a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:13:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(doctor): third review round - quoting, path/URL pieces,
 env names, counts

Leaks closed:
- shell text is split as the shell would (shlex); quoting that does not
  parse is masked whole; SECRET_NAME=... masks everything after "=",
  spaces included
- paths and URLs: the path part of a "/" segment with password symbols is
  judged whole (the query after it piece by piece); base64 pieces next to a
  masked piece are masked; query values are judged by their name (also
  sid, sig, code, session, hash, pass, pwd, otp); relative paths without
  "./" are paths; a file extension no longer hides a grouped key
- plain plural secret names (--tokens, --api-keys) list secrets: only a
  count part (max, cap, per, limit...) makes a number a count
- --password:x and api_key:x; Go-style -pass/-pw; program flags attached
  (-bsession=x) or ending a cluster (-sb x); the argument after a secret
  flag is always its value

Over-masks fixed: UPPER_SNAKE env names judged word by word (0.10% of the
repo's non-secret env names masked, was 1.46% - a regression against
main); model tags, pod names and versions (words with short id parts);
Tailscale tail* hosts, mi- ids, -arn/-fd settings, -D properties, curl
cookie-jar files, QUEUE_MAX_SIZE-like names.

Structure: the generated-token checks are named predicates; magic numbers
are named constants; flag-shape docstrings say which shapes count where.

Tests: relative-path position added and the path/URL skip removed (15
shapes x 5 positions x 4 lengths, tails of 8+ characters count as leaks);
ceilings are the worst over several seeds plus ~2 standard deviations;
the review's cases and every previously uncovered branch are tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
